    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 391 of 2007",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4578\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend chapter 391 of the laws of 2007 relating to directing\nthe law revision commission to make recommendations to the legislature\nconcerning a proposed revision of the alcoholic beverage control law,\nin relation to when certain reports are due\n\n\n PURPOSE OF THE BILL :\nThis bill directs the Law Revision Commission to submit a final report\nby September 30, 2009 regarding proposed revisions of the Alcoholic\nBeverage Control Law.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nThis bill extends the final reporting requirements from June 1, 2009\nto September 30, 2009.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nCurrent law requires the Law Revision Commission to review the\nAlcoholic Beverage Control Law and submit a final report by June 1,\n2009. This bill would extend the timeline for the reporting\nrequirement until September 30, 2009, in order to allow the Law\nRevision Commission more time for examination and therefore a more in\ndepth analysis of the Law. This extension is at the request of the Law\nRevision Commission.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nChapter 391 of the Laws of 2007 required the Law Revision Commission\nto examine the Alcoholic Beverage Control Law and set forth the\nreporting deadlines.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
